Subject: [M156] Fix bugs when ResourceMultiBufferDataProvider::Start fails

Original change's description:
> Fix bugs when ResourceMultiBufferDataProvider::Start fails
>
> When MultiBuffer::AddReader calls ResourceMultiBuffer::CreateWriter,
> ResourceMultiBufferDataProvider::Start is invoked synchronously. If
> UrlIndex has already been destroyed, Start() previously called
> url_data_->Fail() synchronously, which runs
> MultiBufferDataSource::OnRedirected(nullptr) -> StopLoader() and
> destroys the MultiBufferReader while MultiBuffer::AddReader and
> MultiBufferReader::UpdateInternalState are still on the stack.
>
> Post UrlData::Fail asynchronously via task_runner_->PostTask, matching
> the existing asynchronous Terminate() path in Start(). Also check
> stop_signal_received_ with a scoped lock in
> MultiBufferDataSource::SetBitrateTask to match the other posted
> MultiBufferDataSource tasks.
>
> Fixed: 568037533
